  "rules": {
    "ap": "average precision of one tag: AP = sum over the distinct score thresholds, in decreasing order, of (R_n - R_(n-1)) * P_n, with P_n and R_n the precision and recall of the messages scoring at or above the n-th threshold; tied scores form one threshold; not interpolated (sklearn average_precision_score); a tag with no positive is refused; T-invariant (a monotone transform of the logits keeps the ranking)",
    "bootstrap": "A3: one pilot.metrics.bootstrap_weights(n, B, seed) draw of test messages, shared by every model and draw; each replicate's statistic is the mean over draws of (Laya - BERTurk) new-tag macro-AP on the resampled messages; a replicate in which a held-out tag has no positive is undefined (AP is undefined there), counted in n_undefined and left out of the percentile interval; descriptive only, never gated",
    "laya_rows": "a continued run's Laya rows: one random.Random(neg seed) pass over the support and replay rows in selection_train file order (neg seed = training seed = draw seed); per row the old-tag positives, then rng.sample(sorted old-tag negatives, min(neg, n)) (pilot.spike.neg8_rows's shape), then, for a support row only, every label of the held-out tags (positive or negative); a replay row keeps no held-out key",
    "primary": "per new tag, average precision on test by pilot.metrics.AP_RULE on P = sigmoid(logit) (T-invariant: raw T = 1); macro-AP = mean over the six tags; the aggregate is the mean over the three draws; criterion (d) reads the mean over draws of (Laya - BERTurk) macro-AP at k = 10; k = 5 is reported",
    "theta": "A1: each masked base's θ is pilot.metrics.select_theta on its own val dump at T = 1 over all 48 columns (the val rule unchanged: a global θ on val micro-F1, a tag's own θ only with >= 10 val positives); the held-out tags have fewer val positives, so they use the global θ; the base's θ is applied unchanged to the base and to every continued run from it (pilot.fewshot.base_seed_of); nothing is chosen on test",
    "wall": "incremental wall clock of a run, from its own run record (A7): Laya: the sum over its epochs of train_s and save_s, plus load_s and final_save_s; BERTurk: the sum over its epochs of train_s, plus load_s; reported, not gated"
  },
